{
  "case_id": "2011-11-551",
  "document_hash": "9af5804015f1b50b4214d63b01d034b2d8d61fa415877dc45a3dd56f289b0b33",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2011-11-551",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9af5804015f1b50b4214d63b01d034b2d8d61fa415877dc45a3dd56f289b0b33",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9af5804015f1-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "APPEARANCES:\nMARK R. FREEMAN, ESQ., Assistant to the Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.;\non behalf of the Petitioners.\nCARTER G. PHILLIPS, ESQ., Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Respondents."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2011-11-551",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9af5804015f1b50b4214d63b01d034b2d8d61fa415877dc45a3dd56f289b0b33",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9af5804015f1-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We'll hear argument this morning in Case 11-551, Salazar, Secretary of the Interior v. Ramah Navajo Chapter."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2011-11-551",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9af5804015f1b50b4214d63b01d034b2d8d61fa415877dc45a3dd56f289b0b33",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9af5804015f1-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Excuse me, but could the Secretary have done anything else?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2011-11-551",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9af5804015f1b50b4214d63b01d034b2d8d61fa415877dc45a3dd56f289b0b33",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9af5804015f1-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Could the Secretary have done anything else? There's an allegation that the Secretary in fact pays some contractors more than their pro rata share, that it pays some nothing --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2011-11-551",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9af5804015f1b50b4214d63b01d034b2d8d61fa415877dc45a3dd56f289b0b33",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9af5804015f1-0000-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Didn't we have similar language in Cherokee Nation? Didn't we say that that language in Cherokee Nation, which was in the general appropriations statute, although not in each contract, didn't mean that the Secretary could refuse to pay?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2011-11-551",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9af5804015f1b50b4214d63b01d034b2d8d61fa415877dc45a3dd56f289b0b33",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9af5804015f1-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "When the Congressional Budget Office, or whatever agency it is that figures out whether there's a deficit and, if so, of how much, do they look at \"not to exceed,\" and do they take that amount seriously? Or --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2011-11-551",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9af5804015f1b50b4214d63b01d034b2d8d61fa415877dc45a3dd56f289b0b33",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9af5804015f1-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What I don't understand is why the language \"not to exceed\" is any different from Congress appropriating $900,000."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2011-11-551",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9af5804015f1b50b4214d63b01d034b2d8d61fa415877dc45a3dd56f289b0b33",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9af5804015f1-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But that's true of every contract. That's where I'm getting stuck on what your theory is."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2011-11-551",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9af5804015f1b50b4214d63b01d034b2d8d61fa415877dc45a3dd56f289b0b33",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9af5804015f1-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "\"Not to exceed\" has a very significant role to play, Justice Kennedy, because --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2011-11-551",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9af5804015f1b50b4214d63b01d034b2d8d61fa415877dc45a3dd56f289b0b33",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9af5804015f1-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Does the Redbook refer to \"not to exceed\" -- the \"not to exceed\" language?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chamber of Commerce",
      "case_id": "2011-11-551",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9af5804015f1b50b4214d63b01d034b2d8d61fa415877dc45a3dd56f289b0b33",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9af5804015f1-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Chamber of Commerce brief says everybody knows that the contractors are paid in this situation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice BREYER",
      "case_id": "2011-11-551",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9af5804015f1b50b4214d63b01d034b2d8d61fa415877dc45a3dd56f289b0b33",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9af5804015f1-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I don't want to write something that suddenly upsets what is well established."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. PHILLIPS",
      "case_id": "2011-11-551",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9af5804015f1b50b4214d63b01d034b2d8d61fa415877dc45a3dd56f289b0b33",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9af5804015f1-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It is settled that contractors paid from a general appropriation are not barred from recovering for breach of contract, even though the appropriation is exhausted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice KENNEDY",
      "case_id": "2011-11-551",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9af5804015f1b50b4214d63b01d034b2d8d61fa415877dc45a3dd56f289b0b33",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9af5804015f1-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is it your argument that the answer to that is yes?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. PHILLIPS",
      "case_id": "2011-11-551",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9af5804015f1b50b4214d63b01d034b2d8d61fa415877dc45a3dd56f289b0b33",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9af5804015f1-0002-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Our argument here is that there has been a breach of contract, and we're entitled to the damages for the breach of contract, whether those are reliance damages or restitutionary damages, whether we -- whether we're supposed to get what we expected out of the deal, or put back in the position we would have been in --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice ALITO",
      "case_id": "2011-11-551",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9af5804015f1b50b4214d63b01d034b2d8d61fa415877dc45a3dd56f289b0b33",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9af5804015f1-0002-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "For any particular fiscal year, are all of these contracts entered into by a particular date?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. FREEMAN",
      "case_id": "2011-11-551",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9af5804015f1b50b4214d63b01d034b2d8d61fa415877dc45a3dd56f289b0b33",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9af5804015f1-0002-0009",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We adopted this policy in 2006. And one of the principal elements of that policy is that it guarantees that, if -- as long as Congress appropriates as much money as it did in the previous fiscal year, which it generally has, the tribe will get immediately, like within 2 weeks, the exact amount of money that it received in the previous year."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2011-11-551",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "9af5804015f1b50b4214d63b01d034b2d8d61fa415877dc45a3dd56f289b0b33",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9af5804015f1-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FREEMAN: Well, they have a right, Your Honor, in the first instance to the principal promise that's under any ISDA contract, which is we give the amount of money that the Secretary would have provided for the program funds, for operational --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2011-11-551",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "9af5804015f1b50b4214d63b01d034b2d8d61fa415877dc45a3dd56f289b0b33",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9af5804015f1-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 61,
        "start": 61
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: What does each individual tribe have a right to?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2011-11-551",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "9af5804015f1b50b4214d63b01d034b2d8d61fa415877dc45a3dd56f289b0b33",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9af5804015f1-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 62,
        "start": 62
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FREEMAN: We think within a range of reasonable solutions after consultation with the tribes, yes."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2011-11-551",
      "confidence": 0.98,
      "document_hash": "9af5804015f1b50b4214d63b01d034b2d8d61fa415877dc45a3dd56f289b0b33",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9af5804015f1-0003-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 64,
        "start": 64
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2011-11-551",
